  "prompt": "You are an expert JavaScript developer. Create a single-page, standalone HTML document containing a fully playable \"Tango\" logic puzzle game.\n\nSTRICT TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n1. ALL HTML, CSS, and JavaScript must be contained within a single file. No external libraries.\n2. Do NOT output markdown code blocks (```html). Start exactly with <!DOCTYPE html> and end with </html>.\n\nTHEME & VISUALS:\n1. The game must look polished and modern, utilizing a clean, balanced interface.\n2. The grid must be 6x6 cells.\n3. The two playing symbols MUST be the Fire emoji (\ud83d\udd25) and the Ice Cube emoji (\ud83e\uddca).\n4. Constraint markers must clearly sit on the borders between adjacent cells using an Equals sign (=) or a Cross (\u00d7).\n\nCORE GAMEPLAY RULES:\n1. Row and Column Balance: Every row and every column must contain exactly three \ud83d\udd25 and three \ud83e\uddca.\n2. No Three in a Row: You cannot place three identical symbols adjacent to each other horizontally or vertically.\n3. Constraint Markers:\n   - '=' (Equals): The two adjacent cells must contain the same symbol.\n   - '\u00d7' (Cross): The two adjacent cells must contain opposite symbols.\n4. Interactivity: Clicking a cell should cycle its state: Empty -> \ud83d\udd25 -> \ud83e\uddca -> Empty.\n\nBACK-END LOGIC & PROCEDURAL GENERATION SPECS:\nThe game MUST generate a brand new, random, playable board on every page load. Implement the generation using this sequence:\n1. Solution Generation (Backtracking): Write a recursive backtracking function to generate a fully populated, valid 6x6 grid that obeys the Balance and No-Three-In-A-Row rules. \n2. Constraint Placement: Once a valid solved board exists, randomly select 6 to 8 pairs of adjacent cells. If the cells share the same symbol, place an '=' marker between them. If they are different, place an '\u00d7' marker.\n3. Puzzle Creation: After placing constraints, randomly clear (empty) 70% of the cells, leaving a few starting symbols and the constraint markers as hints for the player.\n4. Validation: Implement a \"Check Solution\" button that compares the user's current grid against the underlying rules (Balance, No-Three-In-A-Row, and Constraints). Highlight any errors in red.\n\nEnsure the state management clearly separates the \"solution board\" from the \"player board\", and that markers overlay the grid lines cleanly using CSS absolute positioning or a highly refined Grid layout.\n",
  "rawOutput": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Tango Logic Puzzle</title>\n    <style>\n        :root {\n            --bg-color: #1a1a2e;\n            --panel-color: #16213e;\n            --accent-color: #0f3460;\n            --text-color: #e94560;\n            --fire-color: #ff6b6b;\n            --ice-color: #4ecdc4;\n            --border-color: #2a2a40;\n            --constraint-bg: #2a2a40;\n            --constraint-text: #ffd700;\n        }\n\n        body {\n            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\n            background-color: var(--bg-color);\n            color: white;\n            display: flex;\n            flex-direction: column;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: center;\n            min-height: 100vh;\n            margin: 0;\n            user-select: none;\n        }\n\n        h1 {\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\n            font-weight: 300;\n            letter-spacing: 2px;\n            color: var(--text-color);\n        }\n\n        .game-container {\n            background-color: var(--panel-color);\n            padding: 20px;\n            border-radius: 15px;\n            box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);\n            display: flex;\n            flex-direction: column;\n            align-items: center;\n        }\n\n        .grid {\n            display: grid;\n            grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 60px);\n            grid-template-rows: repeat(6, 60px);\n            gap: 4px;\n            background-color: var(--border-color);\n            border: 4px solid var(--border-color);\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            position: relative;\n        }\n\n        .cell {\n            width: 60px;\n            height: 60px;\n            background-color: var(--panel-color);\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: center;\n            font-size: 28px;\n            cursor: pointer;\n            position: relative;\n            transition: background-color 0.2s;\n        }\n\n        .cell:hover {\n            background-color: var(--accent-color);\n        }\n\n        .cell.fire {\n            color: var(--fire-color);\n            text-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(255, 107, 107, 0.5);\n        }\n\n        .cell.ice {\n            color: var(--ice-color);\n            text-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(78, 205, 196, 0.5);\n        }\n\n        /* Constraint Markers */\n        .constraint {\n            position: absolute;\n            width: 20px;\n            height: 20px;\n            background-color: var(--constraint-bg);\n            color: var(--constraint-text);\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: center;\n            font-size: 14px;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            border-radius: 50%;\n            z-index: 10;\n            pointer-events: none; /* Let clicks pass through to cells */\n        }\n\n        .constraint.right {\n            right: -12px;\n            top: 50%;\n            transform: translateY(-50%);\n        }\n\n        .constraint.bottom {\n            bottom: -12px;\n            left: 50%;\n            transform: translateX(-50%);\n        }\n\n        /* Error Highlighting */\n        .cell.error {\n            background-color: rgba(233, 69, 96, 0.2);\n            animation: shake 0.3s;\n        }\n\n        @keyframes shake {\n            0% { transform: translateX(0); }\n            25% { transform: translateX(-2px); }\n            50% { transform: translateX(2px); }\n            75% { transform: translateX(-2px); }\n            100% { transform: translateX(0); }\n        }\n\n        .controls {\n            margin-top: 20px;\n            display: flex;\n            gap: 15px;\n        }\n\n        button {\n            padding: 10px 20px;\n            border: none;\n            border-radius: 5px;\n            font-size: 16px;\n            cursor: pointer;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            transition: transform 0.1s, opacity 0.2s;\n        }\n\n        button:active {\n            transform: scale(0.95);\n        }\n\n        .btn-new {\n            background-color: var(--accent-color);\n            color: white;\n        }\n\n        .btn-check {\n            background-color: var(--text-color);\n            color: white;\n        }\n\n        .status {\n            margin-top: 15px;\n            height: 24px;\n            font-size: 14px;\n            color: #ccc;\n        }\n\n        .instructions {\n            margin-top: 20px;\n            font-size: 14px;\n            color: #aaa;\n            text-align: center;\n            max-width: 400px;\n            line-height: 1.5;\n        }\n\n        @media (max-width: 500px) {\n            .grid {\n                grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 45px);\n                grid-template-rows: repeat(6, 45px);\n            }\n            .cell {\n                width: 45px;\n                height: 45px;\n                font-size: 20px;\n            }\n            .constraint {\n                width: 14px;\n                height: 14px;\n                font-size: 10px;\n            }\n            .constraint.right { right: -10px; }\n            .constraint.bottom { bottom: -10px; }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n    <h1>TANGO</h1>\n    \n    <div class=\"game-container\">\n        <div id=\"grid\" class=\"grid\">\n            <!-- Grid generated by JS -->\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"controls\">\n            <button class=\"btn-new\" onclick=\"initGame()\">New Puzzle</button>\n            <button class=\"btn-check\" onclick=\"checkSolution()\">Check Solution</button>\n        </div>\n        <div id=\"status\" class=\"status\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"instructions\">\n        <strong>Rules:</strong><br>\n        1. Each row and column must have exactly 3 Fire (\ud83d\udd25) and 3 Ice (\ud83e\uddca).<br>\n        2. No three identical symbols in a row (horizontally or vertically).<br>\n        3. <strong>=</strong> means neighbors are the same.<br>\n        4. <strong>\u00d7</strong> means neighbors are different.<br>\n        <strong>Click a cell to cycle:</strong> Empty \u2192 \ud83d\udd25 \u2192 \ud83e\uddca \u2192 Empty.\n    </div>\n\n    <script>\n        // --- Game Constants & State ---\n        const GRID_SIZE = 6;\n        const SYMBOLS = {\n            EMPTY: 0,\n            FIRE: 1,\n            ICE: 2\n        };\n        \n        let solutionBoard = [];\n        let playerBoard = [];\n        let constraints = {\n            h: [], // Horizontal constraints\n            v: []  // Vertical constraints\n        };\n\n        // --- Core Logic: Generator ---\n\n        function isValid(board, row, col, val) {\n            // Check Row Balance\n            let rowCount = 0;\n            let rowStreak = 0;\n            for (let c = 0; c < GRID_SIZE; c++) {\n                if (board[row][c] === val) rowCount++;\n                if (board[row][c] === val) rowStreak++;\n                else rowStreak = 0;\n                if (rowStreak >= 3) return false;\n            }\n            if (rowCount >= 3) return false;\n\n            // Check Col Balance\n            let colCount = 0;\n            let colStreak = 0;\n            for (let r = 0; r < GRID_SIZE; r++) {\n                if (board[r][col] === val) colCount++;\n                if (board[r][col] === val) colStreak++;\n                else colStreak = 0;\n                if (colStreak >= 3) return false;\n            }\n            if (colCount >= 3) return false;\n\n            return true;\n        }\n\n        function solve(board, row, col) {\n            if (row === GRID_SIZE) return true; // Solved\n            if (col === GRID_SIZE) return solve(board, row + 1, 0); // Next row\n\n            // Try Fire\n            if (isValid(board, row, col, SYMBOLS.FIRE)) {\n                board[row][col] = SYMBOLS.FIRE;\n                if (solve(board, row, col + 1)) return true;\n                board[row][col] = SYMBOLS.EMPTY;\n            }\n\n            // Try Ice\n            if (isValid(board, row, col, SYMBOLS.ICE)) {\n                board[row][col] = SYMBOLS.ICE;\n                if (solve(board, row, col + 1)) return true;\n                board[row][col] = SYMBOLS.EMPTY;\n            }\n\n            return false;\n        }\n\n        function generateSolution() {\n            let board = Array(GRID_SIZE).fill().map(() => Array(GRID_SIZE).fill(SYMBOLS.EMPTY));\n            // Randomize starting bias to ensure variety\n            if (Math.random() > 0.5) board[0][0] = SYMBOLS.FIRE;\n            else board[0][0] = SYMBOLS.ICE;\n            \n            solve(board, 0, 0);\n            return board;\n        }\n\n        function generateConstraints(board) {\n            let hConstraints = Array(GRID_SIZE).fill().map(() => Array(GRID_SIZE - 1).fill(0));\n            let vConstraints = Array(GRID_SIZE - 1).fill().map(() => Array(GRID_SIZE).fill(0));\n\n            // 1. Determine all valid constraints\n            let validConstraints = [];\n\n            for (let r = 0; r < GRID_SIZE; r++) {\n                for (let c = 0; c < GRID_SIZE - 1; c++) {\n                    let type = (board[r][c] === board[r][c+1]) ? '=' : 'x';\n                    validConstraints.push({ r, c, type, axis: 'h' });\n                }\n            }\n\n            for (let r = 0; r < GRID_SIZE - 1; r++) {\n                for (let c = 0; c < GRID_SIZE; c++) {\n                    let type = (board[r][c] === board[r+1][c]) ? '=' : 'x';\n                    validConstraints.push({ r, c, type, axis: 'v' });\n                }\n            }\n\n            // 2. Randomly select 6 to 8 constraints\n            let numConstraints = Math.floor(Math.random() * 3) + 6; // 6, 7, or 8\n            let selected = [];\n            \n            // Shuffle and pick\n            validConstraints.sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5);\n            for (let i = 0; i < Math.min(numConstraints, validConstraints.length); i++) {\n                selected.push(validConstraints[i]);\n            }\n\n            // 3. Populate constraint arrays\n            selected.forEach(c => {\n                if (c.axis === 'h') hConstraints[c.r][c.c] = c.type;\n                else vConstraints[c.r][c.c] = c.type;\n            });\n\n            return { h: hConstraints, v: vConstraints };\n        }\n\n        function createPuzzle(solution, constraintsData) {\n            // Deep copy solution\n            let puzzle = solution.map(row => [...row]);\n            \n            // Clear 70% of cells\n            let totalCells = GRID_SIZE * GRID_SIZE;\n            let cellsToClear = Math.floor(totalCells * 0.7);\n            let cleared = 0;\n\n            while (cleared < cellsToClear) {\n                let r = Math.floor(Math.random() * GRID_SIZE);\n                let c = Math.floor(Math.random() * GRID_SIZE);\n                if (puzzle[r][c] !== SYMBOLS.EMPTY) {\n                    puzzle[r][c] = SYMBOLS.EMPTY;\n                    cleared++;\n                }\n            }\n            return puzzle;\n        }\n\n        // --- Rendering & Interaction ---\n\n        function renderGrid() {\n            const gridEl = document.getElementById('grid');\n            gridEl.innerHTML = '';\n\n            for (let r = 0; r < GRID_SIZE; r++) {\n                for (let c = 0; c < GRID_SIZE; c++) {\n                    const cell = document.createElement('div');\n                    cell.className = 'cell';\n                    cell.dataset.r = r;\n                    cell.dataset.c = c;\n                    \n                    // Render Symbol\n                    const val = playerBoard[r][c];\n                    if (val === SYMBOLS.FIRE) {\n                        cell.textContent = '\ud83d\udd25';\n                        cell.classList.add('fire');\n                    } else if (val === SYMBOLS.ICE) {\n                        cell.textContent = '\ud83e\uddca';\n                        cell.classList.add('ice');\n                    }\n\n                    // Render Constraints (Right)\n                    if (c < GRID_SIZE - 1 && constraints.h[r][c] !== 0) {\n                        const cons = document.createElement('span');\n                        cons.className = 'constraint right';\n                        cons.textContent = constraints.h[r][c];\n                        cell.appendChild(cons);\n                    }\n\n                    // Render Constraints (Bottom)\n                    if (r < GRID_SIZE - 1 && constraints.v[r][c] !== 0) {\n                        const cons = document.createElement('span');\n                        cons.className = 'constraint bottom';\n                        cons.textContent = constraints.v[r][c];\n                        cell.appendChild(cons);\n                    }\n\n                    cell.addEventListener('click', () => handleCellClick(r, c));\n                    gridEl.appendChild(cell);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        function handleCellClick(r, c) {\n            const current = playerBoard[r][c];\n            let next = current + 1;\n            if (next > 2) next = 0; // Cycle: 0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 0\n            playerBoard[r][c] = next;\n            renderGrid();\n            // Remove error styling on interaction\n            document.querySelectorAll('.cell').forEach(el => el.classList.remove('error'));\n            document.getElementById('status').textContent = \"\";\n        }\n\n        function checkSolution() {\n            let errors = [];\n            let errorCells = new Set(); // Store \"r,c\" strings\n\n            // 1. Check Balance & 3-in-a-row (Rows)\n            for (let r = 0; r < GRID_SIZE; r++) {\n                let fireCount = 0;\n                let iceCount = 0;\n                let streak = 0;\n                let lastVal = -1;\n\n                for (let c = 0; c < GRID_SIZE; c++) {\n                    const val = playerBoard[r][c];\n                    if (val === SYMBOLS.FIRE) fireCount++;\n                    if (val === SYMBOLS.ICE) iceCount++;\n\n                    if (val !== lastVal) {\n                        streak = 1;\n                    } else {\n                        streak++;\n                        if (streak === 3) errorCells.add(`${r},${c}`);\n                    }\n                    lastVal = val;\n                }\n                if (fireCount !== 3) {\n                    for(let c=0; c<GRID_SIZE; c++) if(playerBoard[r][c] === SYMBOLS.FIRE) errorCells.add(`${r},${c}`);\n                }\n                if (iceCount !== 3) {\n                    for(let c=0; c<GRID_SIZE; c++) if(playerBoard[r][c] === SYMBOLS.ICE) errorCells.add(`${r},${c}`);\n                }\n            }\n\n            // 2. Check Balance & 3-in-a-row (Cols)\n            for (let c = 0; c < GRID_SIZE; c++) {\n                let fireCount = 0;\n                let iceCount = 0;\n                let streak = 0;\n                let lastVal = -1;\n\n                for (let r = 0; r < GRID_SIZE; r++) {\n                    const val = playerBoard[r][c];\n                    if (val === SYMBOLS.FIRE) fireCount++;\n                    if (val === SYMBOLS.ICE) iceCount++;\n\n                    if (val !== lastVal) {\n                        streak = 1;\n                    } else {\n                        streak++;\n                        if (streak === 3) errorCells.add(`${r},${c}`);\n                    }\n                    lastVal = val;\n                }\n                if (fireCount !== 3) {\n                    for(let r=0; r<GRID_SIZE; r++) if(playerBoard[r][c] === SYMBOLS.FIRE) errorCells.add(`${r},${c}`);\n                }\n                if (iceCount !== 3) {\n                    for(let r=0; r<GRID_SIZE; r++) if(playerBoard[r][c] === SYMBOLS.ICE) errorCells.add(`${r},${c}`);\n                }\n            }\n\n            // 3. Check Constraints\n            // Horizontal\n            for (let r = 0; r < GRID_SIZE; r++) {\n                for (let c = 0; c < GRID_SIZE - 1; c++) {\n                    let cons = constraints.h[r][c];\n                    if (cons !== 0) {\n                        let val1 = playerBoard[r][c];\n                        let val2 = playerBoard[r][c+1];\n                        if (val1 === SYMBOLS.EMPTY || val2 === SYMBOLS.EMPTY) continue; // Ignore empty cells\n\n                        if (cons === '=' && val1 !== val2) {\n                            errorCells.add(`${r},${c}`);\n                            errorCells.add(`${r},${c+1}`);\n                        } else if (cons === 'x' && val1 === val2) {\n                            errorCells.add(`${r},${c}`);\n                            errorCells.add(`${r},${c+1}`);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            // Vertical\n            for (let r = 0; r < GRID_SIZE - 1; r++) {\n                for (let c = 0; c < GRID_SIZE; c++) {\n                    let cons = constraints.v[r][c];\n                    if (cons !== 0) {\n                        let val1 = playerBoard[r][c];\n                        let val2 = playerBoard[r+1][c];\n                        if (val1 === SYMBOLS.EMPTY || val2 === SYMBOLS.EMPTY) continue;\n\n                        if (cons === '=' && val1 !== val2) {\n                            errorCells.add(`${r},${c}`);\n                            errorCells.add(`${r+1},${c}`);\n                        } else if (cons === 'x' && val1 === val2) {\n                            errorCells.add(`${r},${c}`);\n                            errorCells.add(`${r+1},${c}`);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            // Apply Visuals\n            const cells = document.querySelectorAll('.cell');\n            cells.forEach(cell => {\n                const r = cell.dataset.r;\n                const c = cell.dataset.c;\n                if (errorCells.has(`${r},${c}`)) {\n                    cell.classList.add('error');\n                }\n            });\n\n            // Status Message\n            const statusEl = document.getElementById('status');\n            if (errorCells.size === 0) {\n                statusEl.textContent = \"Perfect! Solution is valid.\";\n                statusEl.style.color = \"#4ecdc4\";\n            } else {\n                statusEl.textContent = `${errorCells.size} cell(s) contain errors.`;\n                statusEl.style.color = \"#e94560\";\n            }\n        }\n\n        function initGame() {\n            solutionBoard = generateSolution();\n            constraints = generateConstraints(solutionBoard);\n            playerBoard = createPuzzle(solutionBoard, constraints);\n            renderGrid();\n            document.getElementById('status').textContent = \"\";\n            document.querySelectorAll('.cell').forEach(el => el.classList.remove('error'));\n        }\n\n        // Start\n        initGame();\n\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>",
